              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LAURELP52"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made these for Christmas, along with several other cookies. THESE were gone first! I had to leave out the nuts and thought it would look more festive with the coconut sprinkled on top. I cut them into diamond shapes. A friend even wanted some to take home!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jessaca"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The only change that I made was that I cooked the crust for only 10 min. After reading previous reviews, I decided to try that. These turned out great! I used fresh apricots from my tree. I would def make these again.",
            "datePublished": "2019-06-08T04:34:13.383Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ann Stafford"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Instead of boiling the apricots in 1 c of water, I used 1/2 water and 1/4 rum, and used most of the liquid afterwards. I adjusted for the extra wet ingredients by adding 1/4 more of flour to the apricot mixture. I also used walnuts, pecans and the coconut- sweet- but not too much! No added confectioners sugar, I thought it was sweet enough. Increased the heat to 350 to cook the eggs/apricot mixture. My guests loved it!",
            "datePublished": "2018-09-25T16:49:30.370Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Creative Chris"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I thought these were a bit too sweet the first time I made them, so I reduced the brown sugar down to 2/3 cup, and omitted the confectioner's sugar. I also used chopped almonds instead of walnuts as a matter of personal preference. Very good occasional treat!",
            "datePublished": "2012-12-19T20:55:21.437Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "gaia"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is excellent! I did it first just how it said, but I left the walnuts out as my housemate is allergic to nuts. \r\n\r\nSecond time, I spread some apricot jam between the two layers, and soaked the apricots in a coconut-rum liquor overnight instead of boiling them in water for ten minutes. makes it divine!",
            "datePublished": "2005-12-03T13:54:10.170Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Brenda"
            },
            "reviewBody": "After reading a couple of reviews I tweaked this one just a smidge. The crust was just fine. I didn't overbake it. I took it out before it was golden. It was not crispy but suited the dessert. With the main ingredients, I cut down on the brown sugar. I used about 2/3 cups only. These were delicious (not too sweet) and different! I'll be making these again for sure!",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-27T10:50:18.570Z"
          },
